  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116618",
      "title": "SSR and Client-Server Mismatches",
      "lectureOrder": 324,
      "videoOrder": 306,
      "sourceHash": "77bad533ab398f9a576580e44d60b87b4d861dc09c16cd8979b6a14d48d2b81c",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.87,
          "end": 3.93,
          "en": "Now, one problem you might notice here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.93,
          "end": 6,
          "en": "with the current implementation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6,
          "end": 8.94,
          "en": "in this specific application here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.94,
          "end": 12.39,
          "en": "is that if you are on the page of a user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.39,
          "end": 14.61,
          "en": "so that you see the tasks of that user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.61,
          "end": 16.38,
          "en": "if you load this page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.38,
          "end": 20.91,
          "en": "if you visit this path, you get these tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.91,
          "end": 23.01,
          "en": "But if you then navigate to a different user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.01,
          "end": 26.613,
          "en": "and come back, you see a different list of tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.93,
          "end": 30.93,
          "en": "And the reason for that is that after coming back,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.93,
          "end": 34.02,
          "en": "it's actually the tasks from the local storage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.02,
          "end": 36.18,
          "en": "that are showing up here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.18,
          "end": 38.82,
          "en": "But initially, if you reload this page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.82,
          "end": 41.433,
          "en": "it's the server-side rendered tasks list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.48,
          "end": 46.02,
          "en": "And that list, in the end, uses these dummy tasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.02,
          "end": 48.09,
          "en": "that are set up here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.09,
          "end": 51.66,
          "en": "because local storage can't be accessed on the server side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.66,
          "end": 54.513,
          "en": "We made sure that this code doesn't run there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.68,
          "end": 59.01,
          "en": "Now, of course, this code does run on the client side",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.01,
          "end": 61.62,
          "en": "and this tasks signal is updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.62,
          "end": 64.26,
          "en": "with the tasks on the client side therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.26,
          "end": 67.35,
          "en": "and that's why we see those tasks if we then navigate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.35,
          "end": 68.987,
          "en": "around at some point.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.987,
          "end": 72.51,
          "en": "But initially, we don't see those tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.51,
          "end": 75.39,
          "en": "And the reason for that is that I am updating a signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.39,
          "end": 79.59,
          "en": "but the tasks that are displayed here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.59,
          "end": 82.443,
          "en": "are, in the end, loaded with help of a resolver.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.58,
          "end": 85.92,
          "en": "Remember that we have this resolver here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.92,
          "end": 88.59,
          "en": "which reads the signal once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 88.59,
          "end": 91.23,
          "en": "and does not set up a subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 91.23,
          "end": 94.35,
          "en": "to then prepare the tasks for the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.35,
          "end": 97.8,
          "en": "And then those tasks are made available through an input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 97.8,
          "end": 100.233,
          "en": "That's how those tasks are rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.28,
          "end": 102.72,
          "en": "And on the client side,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 102.72,
          "end": 105.09,
          "en": "once the finished page has been received,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.09,
          "end": 107.78999999999999,
          "en": "this resolver does not run again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 107.78999999999999,
          "end": 111.39,
          "en": "so we don't fetch the updated tasks there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.39,
          "end": 116.03999999999999,
          "en": "So for this specific application, we have some code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.03999999999999,
          "end": 118.32300000000001,
          "en": "that actually leads to a bug.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.43,
          "end": 122.61,
          "en": "Now, to fix this bug, it would probably be best",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 122.61,
          "end": 124.8,
          "en": "to use a different data source,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 124.8,
          "end": 127.77,
          "en": "a data source that also works on the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.77,
          "end": 131.01,
          "en": "like a separate backend to which we send requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 131.01,
          "end": 135,
          "en": "with Angular's HTTP client, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 135,
          "end": 138.24,
          "en": "That would make sure that the code runs on the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.24,
          "end": 142.05,
          "en": "and the appropriate data is fetched on the server already,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.05,
          "end": 145.82999999999998,
          "en": "so that we don't have this mismatch between client-side code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 145.82999999999998,
          "end": 147.81,
          "en": "and server-side code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.81,
          "end": 150.12,
          "en": "If you don't want to do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 150.12,
          "end": 154.95,
          "en": "or you can't do that, it would probably be best to get rid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 154.95,
          "end": 156.42000000000002,
          "en": "of that resolver",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 156.42000000000002,
          "end": 159.9,
          "en": "and instead load the tasks in the component based",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 159.9,
          "end": 163.2,
          "en": "on the signal so that when the signal changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 163.2,
          "end": 166.77,
          "en": "which it does here once the tasks have been loaded,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 166.77,
          "end": 169.5,
          "en": "the component is updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 169.5,
          "end": 173.46,
          "en": "This would then probably be a better solution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 173.46,
          "end": 177.39,
          "en": "and that's why attached you find an updated project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 177.39,
          "end": 179.82,
          "en": "that does switch to that approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 179.82,
          "end": 184.38,
          "en": "and that does not have this bug which you're seeing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 184.38,
          "end": 187.29,
          "en": "I'm showing this on purpose here though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 187.29,
          "end": 189.3,
          "en": "because these are things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 189.3,
          "end": 192.21,
          "en": "and potential problems you have to be aware of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 192.21,
          "end": 195.15,
          "en": "when implementing server-side rendering",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 195.15,
          "end": 196.95,
          "en": "because as mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 196.95,
          "end": 200.94,
          "en": "building server-side rendered apps has certain advantages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 200.94,
          "end": 203.01,
          "en": "but it also has disadvantages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 203.01,
          "end": 204.96,
          "en": "and increased complexity",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 204.96,
          "end": 209.28,
          "en": "or extra problems you might run into belong",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 209.28,
          "end": 212.85,
          "en": "to those potential disadvantages, which is why I wanted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 212.85,
          "end": 215.94299999999998,
          "en": "to show some potential problems here.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
